                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Of all the ATC simulators I've played, I like this one best because it encourages focusing on the task at hand.  I hate to use the term realistic, because I have no idea what a realistic ATC game would actually be like, but it 'feels real' when you're playing it. The planes coming in can get a little overwhelming, but with a little practice it is manageable.  If you like the monotony of managing the safe landing (and take offs) of as many as 20 aircraft on the board at a time, you might like this game.  And it is not expensive to find out.  Kudos to the dev for continuing development and refinement for years after release.",
